abstract: >-
  Rules engine, heuristic and learned agents, tournament harness and complete raw
  results for a systematic study of agent design in the traditional board game
  ṭāb: one-ply lookahead, allocation generation, evaluator calibration, matched
  compute budgets, MCTS and TD(λ) baselines, and a human move-alignment study.
keywords:
  - board games
  - game AI
  - evaluation functions
  - heuristic search
  - Monte Carlo tree search
  - reinforcement learning
  - human-AI alignment
